{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori","id":275147,"title":"Creating GOOD Fomori?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-07T19:52:20-07:00","id":275147,"title":"Creating GOOD Fomori?","content":"I wasn't sure where to post this so I thought I would just put this in the Classic forum. What happens if you use the Life sphere to create a human body, but no soul or mind, and then use the Spirit sphere to bind an Engling or even a Wyldling in to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T21:23:52-07:00","id":275205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori#post275147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't sure where to post this so I thought I would just put this in the Classic forum. What happens if you use the Life sphere to create a human body, but no soul or mind, and then use the Spirit sphere to bind an Engling or even a Wyldling in to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kami, Gorgons and Drones exist there's a book on them they share with Formori<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T21:35:45-07:00","id":275208,"title":"","content":"Except Fomori are the only ones that I remember being created intentionally. If Garou had even the tiniest ability to produce Gorgons or Kami wouldn't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T23:28:10-07:00","id":275223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275208#post275208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Fomori are the only ones that I remember being created intentionally. If Garou had even the tiniest ability to produce Gorgons or Kami wouldn't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they? Garou as a race are really arrogant, why would they even need the help of these possessed persons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T23:51:18-07:00","id":275226,"title":"","content":"My headcanon is that human based Gorgons probably can look even more fucked up than Fomori, because you know, Tzeentch and Wyld share that constant change gimmick. Mutation table for Tzeentch's chosen in the Tome of Corruption is what I use for inspiration. For Fomori it's Khorne's, Nurgle's or Slaneesh's tables.<br /> <br /> Kami should be rather predictable in appearance depending on what elemental or Gaian spirit you bind into them.<br /> <br /> And Mercurial, I would like to point out such bodies probably need soul sbefore binding, because as far as I recall in case of Fomori Banes are melding with bodies and souls of the host', making exorcising them nearly impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-08-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T04:45:19-07:00","id":275342,"title":"","content":"suddenly i was reminded of this <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MvxUiPMfuyU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MvxUiPMfuyU</a> (change the word dalek for Fomori)<br /> but yeah, you got Kami's for that....and if you wanna be an SOB, you got Drones as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T04:47:23-07:00","id":275343,"title":"","content":"In one of the books it talks about the fact that the BSD have a rite that allows them to create Fomori. So really if the Gaian's wanted to, they could do it too. In essence this is exactly what the Corax, Camazotz, Ratkin, and Yeren rites do. They just think more highly of themselves then the others because they are innately more powerful.<br /> <br /> However what you are talking about is slightly different. Them not having a soul/spirit makes a huge difference, but unlike Katsura I don't think that this is an issue at all as far as making it happen. If you were using the Possessed rules then you would in essence have something with no Autonomy from the Trait it serves, and really far more powerful then normal possessed. Without the interference from the host spirit, the new spirit could warp the body into what ever it wanted. This creature would be 100% controlled by the trait it serves and probably extremely volatile, not PC material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T08:35:20-07:00","id":275468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275343#post275343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of the books it talks about the fact that the BSD have a rite that allows them to create Fomori. So really if the Gaian's wanted to, they could do it too. In essence this is exactly what the Corax, Camazotz, Ratkin, and Yeren rites do. They just think more highly of themselves then the others because they are innately more powerful.<br /> <br /> However what you are talking about is slightly different. Them not having a soul/spirit makes a huge difference, but unlike Katsura I don't think that this is an issue at all as far as making it happen. If you were using the Possessed rules then you would in essence have something with no Autonomy from the Trait it serves, and really far more powerful then normal possessed. Without the interference from the host spirit, the new spirit could warp the body into what ever it wanted. This creature would be 100% controlled by the trait it serves and probably extremely volatile, not PC material.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably a lot easier to get a terrible spirit of corruption into a person than it is to try and facilitate the fusion dance with naturae and living beings, the land or the concept of flesh. Kami were often discussed as being living miracles in Possessed as well, so it's probably not a matter of just performing a rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T08:53:52-07:00","id":275475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275468#post275468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably a lot easier to get a terrible spirit of corruption into a person than it is to try and facilitate the fusion dance with naturae and living beings, the land or the concept of flesh. Kami were often discussed as being living miracles in Possessed as well, so it's probably not a matter of just performing a rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agreed on Kami, Possessed lays out that they are more born with their own spirit activated, without the need for a spirit merge. However as far as the Trait specific spirits are concerned, which was where I was really leaning, this empty shell is the perfect host. Since it has no sentience even the Wyld spirits could be manipulated in with little effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T10:17:21-07:00","id":275565,"title":"","content":"Also, the Kuei-Jin have a ritual that allows them to take a corrupted spirit and binds it to a human soul so making a Gaian version should not be that hard to make. Although, I would use similar guidelines to Fomori but with a Gaian tint rather than Wyrm-driven.<br /> Although, TBH, when I read the title, I thought this might be a thread on Fomori builds rather than how to make a non-Wyrm driven Fomori. Or even a thread about how a Fomori can try to do good deeds even though he has a piece of corruption whispering in his ear and sometimes driving him around like Ratatouille.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T11:46:37-07:00","id":275640,"title":"","content":"I looked through Tome of Corruption and needless to say when I'm actually bothered to do it (work comes first) I think I will convert those mutations to Powers that fit for Fomori, and for Gorgons and Drones to some extent (since some Mutations just fit non-Fomors as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or even a thread about how a Fomori can try to do good deeds even though he has a piece of corruption whispering in his ear and sometimes driving him around like Ratatouille </div> </div> </div>Vampires can be at 7 Humanity or higher even with The Beast. So who said some rare Fomori cannot rail against his or her affliction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T12:53:15-07:00","id":275688,"title":"","content":"The difference is of course that while Banes desire to possess mortals, other triatic spirits generally do not. It's no good doing a Rite, if no spirits bother showing up, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T13:23:03-07:00","id":275706,"title":"","content":"Bribe them or cajole them in some way, in other words","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T15:14:23-07:00","id":275803,"title":"","content":"Side note: The paradigm of a human body with all the parts in place but no mind is weird to me, because the mind is a part of the body. Would not such a body simply have a mind that the Mage had no control over? Completely excising it to have a meat puppet seems like it would require Mind to disconnect the concepts magically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275706#post275706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bribe them or cajole them in some way, in other words</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyldlings explicitly do not practice chiminage, so there's no real bribing them as such, and canonically, they don't have anything to do with humans in this regard. Weaver-spirits, meanwhile, don't just messily merge with a subject. They have to be specially bound together after the subject wishes to merge with the OneSong, which requires a trip to an Umbral space and supervision by a much more powerful Weaver-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T16:48:40-07:00","id":275863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275226#post275226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mercurial, I would like to point out such bodies probably need soul sbefore binding, because as far as I recall in case of Fomori Banes are melding with bodies and souls of the host', making exorcising them nearly impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have distinct memories that empty soulless bodies created (or caused) by mages are at risk of being possessed by banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T16:53:58-07:00","id":275868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275863#post275863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have distinct memories that empty soulless bodies created (or caused) by mages are at risk of being possessed by banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only the ones created by mages. Those cloned &quot;Bunyip&quot; turned out to suffer that fate as well, iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T17:59:45-07:00","id":275912,"title":"","content":"Essentially this would be making a fetish. To create a fetish that works properly, the spirit has to assent to the binding; most spirits will not be bound to an object that doesn't suit their tastes or agenda. an empty human body... really wouldn't &quot;do it&quot; for most spirits. You could use the spirit Sphere to force the issue, but then you've got yourself a cursed fetish... or in other words a spirit-powered magical being that hates you and wants to be freed from its imprisonment.<br /> <br /> Most of the sort of spirits that would happily accept the deal are those with the Possession charm - almost all of those are banes, and the remainder are things like disease-spirits, spirits of insanity, and the like.<br /> <br /> Now, of course... this is the Werewolf perspective talking. In mage, every spirit is a unique and individual thing that interacts wit hthe mage on a personal, one-on-one level. So in a straight mage game, there's nothing stopping you from getting some spirit or other to take up residence in a human body you happen to have lying around - in fat maybe that's how you came by your familiar, or something - and in fact I would use the Familiar rules from the Forged by dragon Fire book to represent such a being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 10-08-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:04:15-07:00","id":276014,"title":"","content":"You may be right on using the Familiar rules, but Familiars are highly dependent beings, needing to be constantly fed Quint to survive. I was thinking something a little more out of Possessed, something a bit more self sufficient that could grow as time went on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:15:48-07:00","id":276019,"title":"","content":"well, the thing with possessed characters is that they DO have a human (or other...) spirit, which the possessing spirit bonds with. Whether it's a bane making a fomori, or a Gaian spirit making a kami, the human soul / spirit is still there, entwined with, or dominated by, the possessing spirit.<br /> <br /> An empty vessel like you're saying would likely need something to &quot;fill the gap&quot; - i think that's why familiars need that constant feeding of quintessence, to make up for the lack of an entwined soul for the spirit to draw its energy from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:24:28-07:00","id":276023,"title":"","content":"That's an excellent point and I had not considered that. So the human or animal soul grounds the spirit into this world, allowing it to blend the natural with the supernatural. It figures that you would have to be a master of Spirit to create the spirit fueled shock troops of the Triat and Gaia.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wonder what would happen if you shoved a powerful Wraith in a human husk along with an Engling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 10-08-2014, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T20:57:38-07:00","id":276042,"title":"","content":"While I do not own Possessed I do own Freak Legions and the latter does briefly touch upon the idea of &quot;good&quot; Formori. Specifically those Fomori who are naturally born, usually due to exposure to high levels of Wyrm taint in utero. While they are born with a Bane they are still capable of free will, and the book mentions that some have been known to reject their natural predilections and pursue more noble destinies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T22:03:07-07:00","id":276065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=276023#post276023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I wonder what would happen if you shoved a powerful Wraith in a human husk along with an Engling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know but I suspect the result would be moist and lumpy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T04:24:33-07:00","id":276168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=276023#post276023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an excellent point and I had not considered that. So the human or animal soul grounds the spirit into this world, allowing it to blend the natural with the supernatural. It figures that you would have to be a master of Spirit to create the spirit fueled shock troops of the Triat and Gaia.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wonder what would happen if you shoved a powerful Wraith in a human husk along with an Engling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would get a Risen with additional Possessed like powers, a lot like the fomori that come from a vampire that becomes possessed. Definitely not something I would want to have to deal with in character. Risen are already one of the hardest things to kill in cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T12:08:12-07:00","id":276546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=276042#post276042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do not own Possessed I do own Freak Legions and the latter does briefly touch upon the idea of &quot;good&quot; Formori. Specifically those Fomori who are naturally born, usually due to exposure to high levels of Wyrm taint in utero. While they are born with a Bane they are still capable of free will, and the book mentions that some have been known to reject their natural predilections and pursue more noble destinies.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are so few ferectoi with ethical fiber in existence that a PC that numbers among them is likely the only one in the world. Also, they aren't just born with taint, they're produced when a breeder bane rapes sleeping humans to get their gametes. It then produces a ferectoi baby and ensconces it in a home like the cuckoo do, typically a home of wealth and privilege. They're known as the Princes of Fomori for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T12:31:11-07:00","id":276571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, they aren't just born with taint, they're produced when a breeder bane <b>rapes</b> sleeping humans to get their gametes. It then produces a ferectoi baby and ensconces it in a home like the cuckoo do, typically a home of wealth and privilege. They're known as the Princes of Fomori for a reason. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://randomc.net/image/ALDNOAH%20ZERO/ALDNOAH%20ZERO%20-%2009%20-%2022.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> It's giving me pre-20 era PTSD bouts. ;_;<br /> <br /> But realtalk, I would accept the challenge with GM interested actually in running W20 for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T13:00:20-07:00","id":276596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=276571#post276571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's giving me pre-20 era PTSD bouts. ;_;</div> </div> </div> </div>That detail of the ferectoi has not been changed in W20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But realtalk, I would accept the challenge with GM interested actually in running W20 for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot; </div> </div> </div>It'd take more effort than most have, seeing as how they have a maximum Autonomy, and thus Willpower, of 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T13:13:00-07:00","id":276599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That detail of the ferectoi has not been changed in W20. </div> </div> </div>*PSTD intensifies*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd take more effort than most have, seeing as how they have a maximum Autonomy, and thus Willpower, of 5. </div> </div> </div>Paarthunax managed, I will too. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T18:13:40-07:00","id":276877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=276546#post276546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are so few ferectoi with ethical fiber in existence that a PC that numbers among them is likely the only one in the world. Also, they aren't just born with taint, they're produced when a breeder bane rapes sleeping humans to get their gametes. It then produces a ferectoi baby and ensconces it in a home like the cuckoo do, typically a home of wealth and privilege. They're known as the Princes of Fomori for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think this is something else besides ferectoi. Nosferatu Revised, IIRC, mentions how sometimes (insert their name for fomori which I can't remember offhand) get together in the sewers, or drags a human down their with them, make a baby, and sometimes the baby is a fomori as well. It has been a while since I read it though, so I will have to review that book before I can be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T04:14:45-07:00","id":277088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=276877#post276877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I think this is something else besides ferectoi. Nosferatu Revised, IIRC, mentions how sometimes (insert their name for fomori which I can't remember offhand) get together in the sewers, or drags a human down their with them, make a baby, and sometimes the baby is a fomori as well. It has been a while since I read it though, so I will have to review that book before I can be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Fomori families, they have access to the same rite as the BSD (Rite of Becoming I think its called) which allows them to attract and bind a bane to a member of the family. This typically doesn't happen at birth though, the rite is performed after the child reaches puberty. Can't remember if this is touched on in the Possessed book but I know it gets talked about in Freak Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T07:50:29-07:00","id":277225,"title":"","content":"I am sure there are many ways for the Wyrm to breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:21:33-07:00","id":277480,"title":"","content":"Couldn't you theoretically have self-perpetuating Kami families like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T13:18:14-07:00","id":277520,"title":"","content":"Maybe back when Gaia was stronger and the Apis were still around. Apparently creating creatures who can breed true is no mean feat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T14:57:11-07:00","id":277578,"title":"","content":"My greatest problem with the Possessed book is actually with Autonomy affecting Willpower as that system while theoretically fine doesn't actually work especially considering the Ferectoi who have usually been given WP scores of 9 or so when given as NPC's. They are supposed to be strong willed and in tune with who they are as they have always been that way. They were born Fomori so there is no great struggle between the host and the possessor the urges felt feel natural not forced, and since they are quite capable at masquerading as humans, rich high profile ones at that, it seems they still are able to hold back those urges, which requires WP to do.<br /> Personally I might use Autonomy rules for random Possessions but I would throw them out when it comes to Ferectoi, these are not the easily dominated, or Dominated, types these are the cold blooded bastards that can remain calm even if they are at the same time ripping your hearth out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T20:59:00-07:00","id":277830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=277578#post277578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My greatest problem with the Possessed book is actually with Autonomy affecting Willpower as that system while theoretically fine doesn't actually work especially considering the Ferectoi who have usually been given WP scores of 9 or so when given as NPC's. They are supposed to be strong willed and in tune with who they are as they have always been that way. They were born Fomori so there is no great struggle between the host and the possessor the urges felt feel natural not forced, and since they are quite capable at masquerading as humans, rich high profile ones at that, it seems they still are able to hold back those urges, which requires WP to do.<br /> Personally I might use Autonomy rules for random Possessions but I would throw them out when it comes to Ferectoi, these are not the easily dominated, or Dominated, types these are the cold blooded bastards that can remain calm even if they are at the same time ripping your hearth out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;no struggle or conflict&quot; isn't really true. It's more that the ferectoi rarely, if ever, learn to ever struggle or come to blows with their bane-impulses, or comprehend why they should. Never being born into a normal human existence means that they have no experience with a normal, human existence and don't know about facets of it except insofar as they know enough about others to manipulate them.<br /> <br /> Autonomy definitely could use tuning-up, though. Probably just by kneecapping the rating of Willpower as it applies to resisting the wants of the bane, and remaining high against outside influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T00:17:12-07:00","id":277959,"title":"","content":"That is exactly what I mean with no struggle or conflict the Ferectoi being born as they are have no reason to struggle against the Bane except at best channeling those impulses for a better time or target. The Struggle could be there but it doesn't really occur to them as the Bane is a natural part of who they are.<br /> <br /> And I agree Autonomy limiting your willpower in regards to the Bane is pretty reasonable and understandable it limiting your Permanent WP as it currently does is not really working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T02:24:46-07:00","id":278030,"title":"","content":"For Kotomine Kirei and Paarthunaax, if we go with comparisons to another media, leaning towards evil was inherent part of their existence. Kotomine tried to live an upstanding live remarkably long until Gilgamesh convinced him to be true to himself (and he still is more tragic figure than a villain). For the latter, concepts of ambition and cruelty were inherent part of existence yet he managed to supress that part of existence even if it means daily struggle to not revert.<br /> <br /> Ferectoi could uphold morality in clash with their nature, but basically such person would need to have both strong conviction and mental discipline. And possibly by chance or another twist of fate not end up in the care of Wyrm-tainted mentors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T10:01:11-07:00","id":278198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=278030#post278030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ferectoi could uphold morality in clash with their nature, but basically such person would need to have both strong conviction and mental discipline. And possibly by chance or another twist of fate not end up in the care of Wyrm-tainted mentors.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems pretty unlikely. Possession isn't something you can just 'power through.' These people have evil spirits infesting them since before they were born. How would such a person develop strong convictions without those virtues being influenced by the ravening, depraved Wyrm monster coiled around their soul? I think a person like that might learn to, at best, occasionally mitigate the unwholesome drives and imperatives they experience, but Mockeries are possessed. Possessed work in tandem, the lines between spirit and host blurring both physically and mentally.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am not sure a Ferectoi would even realize their desires were wrong or perverse. They have never known an existence devoid of the Wyrm's presence, so where is that desire to uphold morality coming from? How could they even consider a code of conduct that was not informed by the omnipresent banes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-11-2014, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T11:22:00-07:00","id":278228,"title":"","content":"Shielding myself from the inherent corruption of Freak Legion - Player's Guide to Fomori with a rite honoring Lord Sigmar, I sifted through the blasphemous lore from depths of 90s. And here what I got:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Ferectoi look look and act human, but they are far from it. Most hold humanistic interests and live like any other rich and powerful human. However, they are constantly at odds with themselves, enduring an inner struggle between their humanity and their Wyrm-nature. The Wyrm <b>almost </b>always wins out&quot;<br /> <br /> Another fragment:<br /> <br /> &quot;However, sometimes you have doubts, a voice within you struggles against this evil&quot;<br /> <br /> Let that sink in that there was left a glimmer of hope even for such beings.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T15:22:36-07:00","id":278421,"title":"","content":"Good citations- I was talking about <i>why</i> the Wyrm urges almost always win. And when they don't, where does that leave the Mockery? I don't think the creature would go on to develop a moral center in any normative sense. I see this less as a 'glimmer of hope that the possessed might find redemption,'and more of a 'they might, if they are lucky, summon the alacrity to jump in front of an oncoming train.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T03:26:29-07:00","id":278702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'they might, if they are lucky, summon the alacrity to jump in front of an oncoming train.' </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, aforementioned Kotomine Kirei tried to end his life at one point because he was unhappy about inability to feel joy from good deeds he committed and feeling attraction to the suffering of others. And even that indulging his impulses did not ultimately give him happiness:<br /> <br /> &quot;t is a simple story. There is nothing that brings me happiness. It does not matter, let it believing in people or having people believe in me. What other people called happiness did not bring me any joy.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I envy you people. What I sought, but could not obtain. What I obtained, but could not obtain. Many things slipped out between my fingers, no matter what commandment I used&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:59:44-07:00","id":283934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/275147-creating-good-fomori?p=275863#post275863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have distinct memories that empty soulless bodies created (or caused) by mages are at risk of being possessed by banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just banes -- all manner of creatures are attracted to it. Book of madness goes into this.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much like you walking down a street and seeing a brand new ferrari with the keys in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}